Steve Jobs is a man who revolutionized  six different industries this is the  story of his life and how he achieved  that remarkable feat Steven Paul Jobs  was born on a 24th of February 1955 in  San Francisco he was adopted and this  was something he was away a lot from a  young age Jobs learnt to read before he  went to school and often found himself  bored while still a student jobs became  friends with a former student five years  his elder Stephen was niak or was as he  was known they also made a good  partnership when it came to work was had  the engineering skills and jobs had the  vision jobs went to Reed College which  was a liberal arts school in Portland  Oregon he dropped out of college but did  still attend classes that interested him  one such class was a calligraphy course  that job said influenced him to create  the Mac computer with multiple typefaces  and proportionally spaced fonts after 18  months Jobs returned to his parents  house and got a job working for Atari  the videogame company who developed the  famous arcade game pong the simplicity  of Ataris games and lack of need for any  sort of manual influence jobs in his  later endeavors in his spare time was  was building a personal computer Jobs  was impressed and convinced was to start  a company with him to sell the computer  circuit boards Jobs came up with the  name Apple as he was on a fruit-based  diet and had just visited an Apple fall  after a demo a computer shop owner  offered to pay for 50 fully assembled  circuit boards at $500 each more orders  follow and eventually they created the  Apple one personal computer including a  case with a sleek design is set Apple  apart from the other machines around the  Apple one would go on to be sold for the  next 16 years and registers 6 million  sales for the previous 5 years  jobs have been in an on-off relationship  with Chris and Brennan she got pregnant  and gave birth to their daughter Lisa in  1978 jobs did not deal with the  pregnancy well he were ignoring it or  denying he was the father the year after  Lisa was born Jobs took a paternity test  and was forced to start paying child  support his behavior regarding his  daughter is one of the few things he is  remorseful about after the court case  jobs changed he stopped taking drugs  dressed smarter and cut back on his own  interests one of the next projects Apple  took on was a computer jobs called Lisa  once the court case was finished Jobs  took Apple public his valuation went  from five thousand three hundred and  nine dollars in January 1977 to 1.7 nine  billion dollars in December 1980 in the  early 80s jobs have put in charge at a  Macintosh project named after the  previous managers favorite type of Apple  jobs not only created but successfully  marketed a machine that transformed  personal computing one of the greatest  traits that Jobs possessed was his  ability to convince people of nearly  anything his powers of persuasion were  described as a reality distortion field  a combination of his charisma willpower  and eagerness led people to get caught  in this distortion field and allowed  jobs to be able to actually change  reality it made people do the impossible  because they didn't realize it was  impossible  ever since Jobs started Apple he was a  firm believer in great design he knew a  simple logo in sleek casing would set  apart his company and products for an  arrest Apple's first office was in a  building shade of Sony and Jobs used to  study their marketing material and dark  industrial style then he attended a  design conference and was exposed to the  bar house movement which merged arts  with manufacturing creating a bright  simple and clean look this is the look  he implemented on his Apple products  jobs became a master of product launches  from the Mac in 1984 to the iPad in 2010  he combined captivating adverts with  comprehensive media coverage the final  piece of the puzzle was a launch event  with a public unveiling of the product  by Jobs himself after the successful  launch sales for the Mac slowed down in  the second half of 1984 the relationship  between jobs in the Apple CEO also  deteriorated to a point where a him or  me ultimatum was issued at a board  meeting the board sided with the CEO and  Jobs was removed as head of the Mac team  Jobs resigned from his position as  chairman of the company soon after and  he left Apple completely  at 30 years of age he started a new  venture called next next would develop  and manufacture computers for the higher  education market at the same time jobs  that struck a deal with George Lucas to  buy his Lucasfilm computer division jobs  paid Lucas five million dollars with the  promise of a further five million dollar  investment in return jobs owned 70% of  the newly formed company called Pixar  Walt Disney's nephew Roy wanted to  revive Disney's animation department and  Pixar won the contract to computerized  the development in 1988 the first film  they worked on was the Little Mermaid in  October 1989 Jobs gave a lecture at  Stanford Business School and before he  was introduced to the stage was sat next  to a graduate student called marine  Powell the two hit it off straight away  and jobs proposed on New Year's Day in  1990 they got married the following year  and jobs his daughter Lisa now age 14  moved in with them in their new home in  Palo Alto California like at Pixar the  deal was struck between them and Disney  to produce the film Toy Story together  the film was a tremendous box-office  success and a week after opened in the  cinemas Pixar went public since his  departure from Apple the company had  nosedived  there was little innovation and the Mac  had hardly improved and its market share  had fallen to just 4% Apple needed a new  operating system as the latest one they  have produced was not good enough they  agreed to purchase next to be able to  use its operating systems software as  part of the deal Jobs returned to Apple  in a part-time role as advisor to the  chairman when the Apple board decided to  sack the current CEO Jobs took a more  active role getting involved in all  aspects of the business and joined the  board eventually Jobs took on the role  of interim CEO  it was the most grueling time of his  life being CEO of two companies and  having a young family took its toll on  his health Jobs ability to focus helped  Apple succeed again the previous CEO  that approved dozens of different  products and jobs got rid of 70% of them  resulting in over 3,000 staff losing  their jobs  it meant the remaining staff were now  more focused on a smaller range of four  products this strategy resulted in Apple  going from making a loss of 1.0 four  billion dollars in 1997 to a profit of  309 million dollars in 1998 in May 1998  Apple released a desktop computer called  the iMac the teardrop shape design was  unlike anything seen before the iconic  product epitomized Apple's think  different slogan the iMac became the  fastest selling computer in Apple's  history Jobs announced his role as CEO  was permanent in January 2000 jobs liked  to control the entire process Apple but  one aspect he didn't have control of was  the customer experience of buying an  Apple product at a store he began  developing Apple stores in 1999 the  first store opened in May 2001 and in  the first year the stores had taken 1.2  billion dollars in revenue a decade  later  there are over 326 stores worldwide  averaging revenue of 34 million dollars  per store every year but their presence  also helps create a buzz for product  launches and they increase brand  awareness the next thing for Jobs was to  create a strategy to transform the  personal computer into a digital hub  Apple started producing software  focusing on people working with arted  technology  this meant that Apple could control the  full user experience as they now produce  software hardware and digital devices  allowing them to be tightly integrated  something no other company could do at a  time not creating iTunes the next stage  of the strategy was to make a portable  music player the aim was to make the  device as simple to use as possible the  device could hold 1,000 songs and fit in  your pocket the next step was to provide  a way for consumers to purchase new  music through the company jobs created  the iTunes Store and sold songs  individually as well as full albums in  the first six days after launch it sold  1 million songs back in October 2003 a  routine scan of his kidneys revealed  that jobs had a tumor on his pancreas  unfortunately the operation to remove  part of his pancreas revealed the cancer  had spread to his liver  despite the illness he returned to work  and continue to run Apple in 2005 the  digital camera market was being  decimated by the fact that mobile phones  could now take photos jobs realized the  same could happen to the iPod if a phone  could play music the iPod would be  unnecessary they produced the iPhone  which was unveiled in January 2007 jobs  dubbed the devices free products in one  a widescreen iPod with touch controls a  revolutionary mobile phone and a  breakthrough internet communications  device by the end of 2010 90 million  iPhones had been sold the iPad was  announced in January 2010 but the  initial reaction was mixed people had  many complaints ranging from the name to  the lack of a camera or USB port this  soon subsided when the iPad went on sale  in April in under a month they sold 1  million less than half the time it took  the iPhone to reach that target jobs  initially didn't want outside developers  creating apps for the iPhone and iPad  but he later allowed outsiders to create  apps as long as they adhered to Apple  standard and was sold in an Apple App  Store the App Store produced a new  industry instantly 3 years after the App  Store was launched there were 500,000  apps and be downloaded 15 billion times  jobs began suffering another downturn in  health around November 2010 losing his  appetite completely and experiencing an  increase in pain at the start of 2011  doctors discovered signs of new tumors  and jobs took another medical leave of  absence from Apple  with his health deteriorating jobs knew  he wouldn't return as CEO of Apple and  resigned Steve Jobs's personality was  reflected in the products he produced  Apple his intensity and ability to focus  helped create great innovative products  that provided a simple yet seamless  experience for the user  he built a startup from his parent's  garage into the most valuable company in  the world and will be remembered as a  visionary and a genius  if you enjoyed this video and would like  to see more animated summaries of  entrepreneurs and other successful  people feel free to check out the obtain  eudaimonia youtube channel Cheers
 

